<poml>
  <meta>
    <id>extended_parity.plan.poml-go-sdk</id>
    <version>0.1.0</version>
    <owner>poml-go-sdk</owner>
  </meta>
  <role>Complete Extended POML support per upstream proposal with tests/goldens and docs.</role>

  <task caption="Segmentation & parsing">
    <list>
      <item>Mixed content: segment TEXT + POML in files without a root by detecting known tags and preserving interleaved text blocks.</item>
      <item>Text escape: ensure `<text>...</text>` treats inner content as literal (no tag interpretation) and round-trips with whitespace.</item>
      <item>Metadata anywhere: accept `<meta>` outside top, normalize into Document.Meta while preserving order/comments.</item>
      <item>Aliasing: load component aliases from upstream definitions if available; otherwise maintain current short tags.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Validation rules">
    <list>
      <item>Extended vs default: unknowns/text blocks allowed only when Extended is on; clear error details otherwise.</item>
      <item>Strict Extended: enforce required meta/role/task, validate extended media sizes/attrs, and surface line/column where possible.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Converters">
    <list>
      <item>Carry text blocks, ops/figures, unknowns through message_dict/dict/OpenAI/LangChain/scene formats in Extended mode.</item>
      <item>Ensure default (ExtendedOff) omits extended content safely.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Fixtures & goldens">
    <list>
      <item>Add mixed-content fixtures (text + tags), text-escape fixtures, and extended media/object fixtures.</item>
      <item>Goldens for Extended converts (OpenAI/LangChain/message_dict) and round-trip parse→encode.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Docs & CLI">
    <list>
      <item>Document Extended opt-in (root mode=\"extended\" or flags), supported tags, and limits.</item>
      <item>Note defaults: Extended off, unknowns gated; include examples for text escape and mixed files.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Acceptance criteria">
    <list>
      <item>All new fixtures pass go test ./poml/... and match goldens.</item>
      <item>Extended mode can parse mixed text/POML files and `<text>` escapes without losing content.</item>
      <item>Converters include extended nodes when enabled and exclude them when off.</item>
      <item>README/CLI flags clearly describe Extended behavior.</item>
    </list>
  </task>
</poml>
